Q: @Value not working in Spring @Configuration A: <p>If you are using springboot, simply place the application.properties file in <code>src/main/resources/</code> or <code>src/main/resources/config/</code> directory. No need to configure WebConfig, all beans can directly reference properties using @Value.</p>
<p>If not using springboot, you can try the following approach:</p>
<pre><code>@Configuration
@Import(WebConfig.class)
class MyServerConfig {

    @Value(&quot;${server.url}&quot;)
    private String url;
    ...
} 
</code></pre>
<p>Import the WebConfig configuration class in MyServerConfig to make the PropertySourcesPlaceholderConfigurer effective.</p>

Q: Centering a table with text-align center A: <p>You need to calculate the width of the table using javascript/jquery to have a better control with it. Check <a href="https://jsbin.com/tonimul/edit?html,output" rel="nofollow noreferrer">this</a> sample.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>$(document).ready(function() {

  $('#myTable').css({
    width: $('#myTable').outerWidth() + 'px'
  });

});</code></pre>
